# Binaural beats in pink noise during a 30-minute vigilance task (Lane et al. 1998)
#
# A published sensory stimulation protocol, encoded from its source with
# SSTIM terms. It describes the method as the source reports it and asserts
# no effect: evidence about effects is a separate, authored claim (ADR 0027).
# The protocol cites its paper with dct:source instead of naming a framework
# (ADR 0064), its skos:editorialNote says what was read, and a level the
# source reports without a measurement point keeps the source's words in
# sstim:reportedAs at an unstated stage (ADR 0063). Why these protocols exist
# and how they are read: static/ontology/instances/README.md.

@prefix bfo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix obo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix dct:             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix sstim:           <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix sstim-ex:        <https://w3id.org/sstim/exposure#> .
@prefix sstim-v:         <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#> .
@prefix sstim-ref:       <https://w3id.org/sstim/ref/> .
@prefix xsd:             <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix bsclab-protocol: <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/> .
@prefix l1998:           <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/lane-1998-binaural-beats-vigilance#> .


###########################################################################
# 8. Lane, Kasian, Owens and Marsh 1998: binaural beats during a
#    vigilance task. Full text: Materials and Methods.
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:lane-1998-binaural-beats-vigilance a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "Binaural beats in pink noise during a 30-minute vigilance task (Lane et al. 1998)"@en ;
    dct:description "Participants perform a 30-minute visual vigilance task (letters shown once a second for 100 ms, a repeated letter as the target, six targets a minute) on three afternoons, seated in a dimly lit room, while a cassette tape plays through stereo headphones at a level each participant finds comfortable and that masks outside sound. Every tape holds pink noise, flat from 40 to 320 Hz and falling 12 dB per octave above and below, with carrier tones at 100, 200, 250 and 300 Hz set 15 dB above the noise. On the beta tape the 200 Hz tone carries a 16 Hz binaural beat and the 300 Hz tone a 24 Hz beat; on the theta/delta tape the 100 Hz tone carries a 1.5 Hz beat and the 200 and 250 Hz tones 4 Hz beats; the other tones carry none, and all play at once. The first session is training, with a control tape that holds the same sounds and no beats; the beta and theta/delta tapes follow in the second and third sessions in counterbalanced, double-blind order. Participants are told the sound is a uniform background and are not told about the beats. Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techBinauralBeats, sstim-v:techBroadbandNoise ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralPhenomenon sstim-v:phenomenonOscillatoryDynamics ;
    sstim:participantEngagementMode sstim-v:engagementPassiveReceptive ;
    sstim:protocolStudyDesign sstim-v:designControlledTrial ;
    sstim:armAllocation sstim-v:allocationWithinSubject ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation l1998:population ;
    sstim:hasSchedule l1998:schedule ;
    sstim:hasStudyArm l1998:arm-beta, l1998:arm-theta-delta ;
    sstim-ex:hasExposureProfile l1998:beta-profile, l1998:theta-delta-profile, l1998:control-profile ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:LANE_1998 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the full text (Physiology and Behavior 63(2):249-252), Materials and Methods, read 2026-10-15. The comparison is beta against theta/delta, so beta is the experimental arm and theta/delta the active comparator, another frequency; the paper's directional hypothesis was that beta would do better. The control tape is not an arm: it was always played in the first, training session and never compared, so it is kept as that session's sound. The beat signals are sine: each beat is the difference between two pure tones. The carrier tones' level 15 dB above the noise uses the term ADR 0066 added for a level relative to another part of the same sound. The noise's spectrum, flat from 40 to 320 Hz and falling 12 dB per octave above and below, has no SSTIM term and is in the description only. The intended neural phenomenon is the paper's rationale, entrainment of the EEG bands named, which it did not measure."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

l1998:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "Healthy adults aged 19 to 51"@en ;
    dct:description "Twenty-nine of 32 volunteers recruited from the Duke University community completed the protocol: 19 women and 10 men, mean age 32 ± 10 years, in good health, with normal hearing and normal or corrected vision, free of acute illness and medication, and nonsmokers."@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

# Three sessions on different days, at the same time of the afternoon for
# each participant; the first is the training session.
l1998:schedule a sstim:StimulationSchedule ;
    sstim:sessionDurationSeconds "1800.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionsPerDay "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionCount 3 .

l1998:arm-beta a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Beta binaural beats, 16 and 24 Hz"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armExperimental ;
    sstim:armStimulus l1998:beta-stimulus .

l1998:arm-theta-delta a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Theta/delta binaural beats, 1.5 and 4 Hz"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armActiveComparator ;
    sstim:armStimulus l1998:theta-delta-stimulus .

l1998:beta-profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Beta condition: pink noise and tones with 16 and 24 Hz binaural beats, 30 minutes"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel l1998:beta-audio ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

l1998:theta-delta-profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Theta/delta condition: pink noise and tones with 1.5 and 4 Hz binaural beats, 30 minutes"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel l1998:theta-delta-audio ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

l1998:control-profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Training session: the same pink noise and tones without binaural beats, 30 minutes"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel l1998:control-audio ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

l1998:beta-audio a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "Headphone audio: pink noise and tones at 100, 200, 250 and 300 Hz, with binaural beats at 16 and 24 Hz"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementEarLeft, sstim-ex:placementEarRight ;
    sstim-ex:requiresDeviceCapability sstim-ex:capabilityHeadphones, sstim-ex:capabilityStereoSeparation ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternContinuous, sstim-ex:audioNoisePink ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "1800.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude l1998:listening-level, l1998:tone-level ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering l1998:beat-16-rendering, l1998:beat-24-rendering .

l1998:theta-delta-audio a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "Headphone audio: pink noise and tones at 100, 200, 250 and 300 Hz, with binaural beats at 1.5 and 4 Hz"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementEarLeft, sstim-ex:placementEarRight ;
    sstim-ex:requiresDeviceCapability sstim-ex:capabilityHeadphones, sstim-ex:capabilityStereoSeparation ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternContinuous, sstim-ex:audioNoisePink ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "1800.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude l1998:listening-level, l1998:tone-level ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering l1998:beat-1-5-rendering, l1998:beat-4-on-200-rendering, l1998:beat-4-on-250-rendering .

l1998:control-audio a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "Headphone audio: pink noise and the same tones, no binaural beats"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementEarLeft, sstim-ex:placementEarRight ;
    sstim-ex:requiresDeviceCapability sstim-ex:capabilityHeadphones ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternContinuous, sstim-ex:audioNoisePink ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleControlOrSham ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "1800.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude l1998:listening-level, l1998:tone-level .

# Set by each participant: 0 dB above their own comfortable level is that level.
l1998:listening-level a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantityLevelAboveReference ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "0.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitDecibel ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageSubjectRelative ;
    sstim:relativeToParticipantMeasure sstim-v:referenceComfortableLevel ;
    sstim:relativeQuantity sstim-v:quantitySoundPressureLevel ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "Auditory volume was adjusted to a comfortable listening level for the participant that would block perception of external sounds." .

# Set on the tape: the carrier tones sound 15 dB above the pink noise. A level
# between two parts of one recording holds at every stage a playback passes
# through unchanged, so its stage is the configured one, where it was set.
l1998:tone-level a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    rdfs:label "Carrier tones above the pink noise"@en ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantityLevelAboveComponent ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitDecibel ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageConfigured ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "Tapes also contained carrier tones at 100, 200, 250, and 300 Hz, which had amplitudes 15 db above the amplitude of the pink noise." .

l1998:beat-16 a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "16 Hz binaural beat"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSine ;
    sstim:hzMin "16.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "16.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:beta .

l1998:beat-24 a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "24 Hz binaural beat"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSine ;
    sstim:hzMin "24.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "24.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:beta .

l1998:beat-1-5 a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "1.5 Hz binaural beat"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSine ;
    sstim:hzMin "1.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "1.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:delta .

# 4 Hz is the shared bound of SSTIM's delta (0.5 to 4) and theta (4 to 8)
# bands, both inclusive, which is presumably why the authors call this
# condition theta/delta. Both containments are true and both are asserted.
l1998:beat-4 a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "4 Hz binaural beat"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSine ;
    sstim:hzMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:delta, sstim-v:theta .

l1998:beat-16-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "16 Hz binaural beat on the 200 Hz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal l1998:beat-16 ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramFrequency ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismBinauralBeat ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePerceptual ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "200.0"^^xsd:decimal .

l1998:beat-24-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "24 Hz binaural beat on the 300 Hz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal l1998:beat-24 ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramFrequency ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismBinauralBeat ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePerceptual ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "300.0"^^xsd:decimal .

l1998:beat-1-5-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "1.5 Hz binaural beat on the 100 Hz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal l1998:beat-1-5 ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramFrequency ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismBinauralBeat ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePerceptual ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "100.0"^^xsd:decimal .

l1998:beat-4-on-200-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "4 Hz binaural beat on the 200 Hz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal l1998:beat-4 ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramFrequency ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismBinauralBeat ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePerceptual ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "200.0"^^xsd:decimal .

l1998:beat-4-on-250-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "4 Hz binaural beat on the 250 Hz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal l1998:beat-4 ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramFrequency ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismBinauralBeat ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePerceptual ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "250.0"^^xsd:decimal .

l1998:beta-stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Beta binaural-beat condition (Lane et al. 1998)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "stochastic" ;
    sstim:hasSignal l1998:beat-16, l1998:beat-24 ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel l1998:beta-audio ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget l1998:subject .

l1998:theta-delta-stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Theta/delta binaural-beat condition (Lane et al. 1998)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "stochastic" ;
    sstim:hasSignal l1998:beat-1-5, l1998:beat-4 ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel l1998:theta-delta-audio ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget l1998:subject .

l1998:subject a bfo:0000040, obo:NCBITaxon_9606 ;
    rdfs:label "Human participant"@en .
